---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About Us — Nexus Wave Technologies" description="Learn about Nexus Wave Technologies, its founder Kuldeep Kumari Yadav, its products, accessibility mission, spiritual learning work and women safety initiatives.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-shell">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About Nexus Wave Technologies</p>
        <h1>Technology with purpose, accessibility and human responsibility.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Nexus Wave Technologies is an independent, developer-led community creating accessible digital products, spiritual learning experiences and practical support initiatives designed around real human needs.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="/shlok">Explore Geeta Nexus</a>
          <a class="button" href="/women-safety">Women Safety</a>
          <a class="button" href="/contact">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-panel">
        <img src="/assets/founder-desk.jpg" alt="Founder workspace at Nexus Wave Technologies" class="responsive-media" />
        <p class="muted">Independent, accessibility-first product development from India, with a focus on useful technology and direct community impact.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our purpose</p>
        <h2>Build technology that helps people in everyday life.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Nexus Wave Technologies brings together software development, accessibility, AI utilities, spiritual learning and community initiatives under one practical ecosystem. The goal is not simply to publish features, but to make digital experiences easier to use, easier to understand and more useful for the people who rely on them.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
        <h2>People first. Safety first. Accessibility by default.</h2>
        <p class="muted">We treat clear navigation, screen-reader support, keyboard access, respectful communication, privacy-aware data handling and responsible design as core product requirements rather than optional extras.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">What we stand for</p><h2>Two commitments guide the ecosystem.</h2></div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 · Women’s safety, dignity & support</p>
          <h3>Safety should be easier to reach when someone needs help.</h3>
          <p class="muted">Women’s safety is a core priority for Nexus Wave Technologies. We aim to build practical reporting and support pathways that can be reached from the website, Nexus Plus and Geeta Nexus, while respecting privacy, consent and personal choice.</p>
          <p class="muted">Our approach is support-oriented rather than promising outcomes that an independent platform cannot guarantee. When a situation may require emergency, medical or legal intervention, users should be connected to appropriate official or professional resources.</p>
          <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/women-safety">Explore Women Safety</a><a class="button" href="/women-safety#report">Report a concern</a></div>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 · Spiritual growth & learning</p>
          <h3>Make timeless spiritual knowledge easier to access.</h3>
          <p class="muted">Through Geeta Nexus and the website reading experience, we make the Bhagavad Gita easier to read, listen to and explore. Accessibility is especially important here so that people using screen readers and other assistive technologies can participate fully.</p>
          <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/shlok">Read a Shlok</a><a class="button" href="/apps#geeta-nexus">Explore Geeta Nexus</a></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="founder">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Founder & lead developer</p>
        <h2>Kuldeep Kumari Yadav</h2>
        <p class="muted">Nexus Wave Technologies is founded and led by <strong>Kuldeep Kumari Yadav</strong>. The work combines software engineering, product development, accessibility-focused thinking and community initiatives.</p>
        <p class="muted">The aim is simple: build technology that is useful on an ordinary day and meaningful when someone genuinely needs support.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility promise</p>
        <h2>Designed so more people can participate.</h2>
        <p class="muted">We prioritize semantic structure, readable interfaces, keyboard navigation, screen-reader labels, clear controls and reduced-motion support. Accessibility is considered across products, website pages and community experiences.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">What we are building</p><h2>A connected Nexus ecosystem.</h2></div></div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Geeta Nexus</h3>
          <p class="muted">A standalone spiritual learning project focused on the Bhagavad Gita, accessible reading, listening and daily devotional practice.</p>
          <ul class="feature-list"><li>Bhagavad Gita reading experience</li><li>Accessible navigation and screen-reader support</li><li>Daily shlok and spiritual learning tools</li></ul>
          <a class="button" href="/shlok">Open Shlok Reader</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Nexus Plus</h3>
          <p class="muted">An all-in-one platform for AI, media, audio, document, accessibility and everyday utility features.</p>
          <ul class="feature-list"><li>AI assistance and productivity tools</li><li>Audio, media and document utilities</li><li>Access to safety and support pathways</li></ul>
          <a class="button" href="/apps#nexus-plus">Explore Nexus Plus</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Nexus Care</h3>
          <p class="muted">An upcoming wellness-focused initiative intended to support healthier routines, personal organization and specialized guidance resources.</p>
          <ul class="feature-list"><li>Habit and routine support</li><li>Private personal organization</li><li>Specialized wellness resources under development</li></ul>
          <span class="note">Currently in development.</span>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="women-safety">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Women Safety & Respect</p><h2>From awareness to practical support.</h2></div><a class="button primary" href="/women-safety">Open the safety center</a></div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card"><h3>Safe reporting</h3><p class="muted">A dedicated reporting flow is being designed so people can share concerns and request support without turning a website form into a promise of guaranteed intervention.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Safety campaign</h3><p class="muted">Community members can participate in awareness and support initiatives, with evidence standards that discourage fabricated stories and unverifiable claims.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Community support</h3><p class="muted">The wider community can contribute practical guidance, helpful answers and respectful discussion while harmful or hateful content is moderated.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Our ecosystem at a glance</p><h2>Projects and initiatives.</h2></div></div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Project / Initiative</th><th>Focus</th><th>Status</th><th>What it provides</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Geeta Nexus</th><td>Bhagavad Gita & spiritual practice</td><td>Live</td><td>Accessible reading, daily shlok and listening experiences</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Nexus Plus</th><td>Utility, AI, media & safety support</td><td>Live</td><td>Productivity tools, AI features, media utilities and support access</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Nexus Care</th><td>Wellness & routine support</td><td>In development</td><td>Habit, organization and specialized wellness resources</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Women’s Safety Campaign</th><td>Awareness, support & active respect</td><td>Core initiative</td><td>Reporting, campaign participation and community support pathways</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Responsible support</p>
        <h2>We will be clear about what we can and cannot do.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Nexus Wave Technologies is an independent technology initiative, not a police authority, legal service, hospital or emergency response organization. A report submitted through our systems should never replace urgent professional help where that is needed.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Connect with us</p>
        <h2>Ideas, feedback and collaboration are welcome.</h2>
        <p class="muted">For product feedback, accessibility suggestions, partnerships or community initiatives, contact the Nexus Wave Technologies team.</p>
        <p><strong>Founder:</strong> Kuldeep Kumari Yadav</p>
        <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:kuldeepky538@gmail.com">kuldeepky538@gmail.com</a></p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/contact">Contact</a><a class="button" href="/join-team">Join the team</a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>